  "body": "## Summary\n\nIf a fee-on-transfer (FoT) token is configured as the `disputeToken`, the `resolveDispute()` function will permanently revert, leaving the protocol in an unrecoverable bricked state. This occurs because `disputeTree()` records the full `disputeAmount` but the contract receives fewer tokens due to the transfer fee, making it impossible to transfer back the recorded amount during resolution.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n### Root Cause\n\nStep 1 - Dispute Creation (`disputeTree`):\n\n```solidity\nfunction disputeTree(string memory reason) external {\n    if (disputer != address(0)) revert Errors.UnresolvedDispute();\n    if (block.timestamp >= endOfDisputePeriod) revert Errors.InvalidDispute();\n    IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), disputeAmount);\n    disputer = msg.sender;\n    emit Disputed(reason);\n}\n```\n\nWhen a user calls `disputeTree()` with a FoT token:\n- User sends `disputeAmount` tokens (e.g., 1000 tokens)\n- FoT token deducts transfer fee (e.g., 1% = 10 tokens)\n- Contract receives only 990 tokens\n- Contract records `disputer = msg.sender` (no record of actual received amount)\n\nStep 2 - Dispute Resolution (`resolveDispute`) - ALWAYS REVERTS:\n\n```solidity\nfunction resolveDispute(bool valid) external onlyGovernor {\n    if (disputer == address(0)) revert Errors.NoDispute();\n    if (valid) {\n        IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(disputer, disputeAmount);  // Tries to send 1000\n        _revokeTree();\n    } else {\n        IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(msg.sender, disputeAmount); // Tries to send 1000\n        endOfDisputePeriod = _endOfDisputePeriod(uint48(block.timestamp));\n    }\n    disputer = address(0);\n    emit DisputeResolved(valid);\n}\n```\n\nBoth branches attempt to transfer `disputeAmount` (1000 tokens), but:\n- Contract only holds 990 tokens\n- For FoT tokens, the transfer also burns a fee first, further reducing available balance\n- Transfer reverts with \"ERC20: transfer amount exceeds balance\"\n\n### State After Failed Resolution\n\nSince `resolveDispute()` always reverts:\n1. `disputer` remains set to the original disputer address (non-zero)\n2. The dispute cannot be cleared through any mechanism\n3. Protocol enters permanent freeze state\n\n## Impact\n\n### Permanent Protocol Freeze\n\n1. Dispute Cannot Be Resolved:\n- `resolveDispute(true)` reverts - cannot return stake to valid disputer\n- `resolveDispute(false)` reverts - cannot slash stake to governor\n\n2. `disputer` Remains Non-Zero Forever:\n- `resolveDispute()` is the only function that sets `disputer = address(0)`\n- Since it always reverts, `disputer` is permanently set\n\n3. All Tree Updates Blocked:\n```solidity\nfunction updateTree(MerkleTree calldata _tree) external {\n    if (\n        disputer != address(0) ||  // <-- Always true after FoT dispute\n        // ...\n    ) revert Errors.NotTrusted();\n    // ...\n}\n```\nNo new Merkle trees can ever be published.\n\n4. Tree Revocation Blocked:\n```solidity\nfunction revokeTree() external onlyGovernor {\n    if (disputer != address(0)) revert Errors.UnresolvedDispute();  // <-- Always reverts\n    _revokeTree();\n}\n```\n\n5. Claims Frozen on Stale Data:\n- Users can only claim from the old `lastTree`\n- Any new rewards computed off-chain cannot be distributed\n- Protocol becomes permanently non-functional\n\n6. No Recovery Path:\n- `recoverERC20()` cannot help because `resolveDispute()` needs to succeed first to clear `disputer`\n- Even depositing more tokens doesn't help - the FoT token will take fees on the outgoing transfer too\n- Contract upgrade/migration is the only recovery option\n\n### Attack Vector\n\nThis is not a malicious attack - it occurs through legitimate protocol use:\n\n1. Governor sets `disputeToken` to a FoT token (PAXG, some USDT implementations, deflationary tokens)\n2. Honest user notices an incorrect Merkle tree\n3. User calls `disputeTree()` - deposits tokens in good faith\n4. Contract receives fewer tokens than recorded due to transfer fee\n5. Governor attempts to resolve dispute (valid or invalid)\n6. Transaction reverts - protocol is permanently bricked\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\n### Option 1: Track Actual Received Amount\n\n```solidity\n// Add new state variable\nuint256 public disputeStake;\n\nfunction disputeTree(string memory reason) external {\n    if (disputer != address(0)) revert Errors.UnresolvedDispute();\n    if (block.timestamp >= endOfDisputePeriod) revert Errors.InvalidDispute();\n\n    uint256 balanceBefore = IERC20(disputeToken).balanceOf(address(this));\n    IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), disputeAmount);\n    uint256 actualReceived = IERC20(disputeToken).balanceOf(address(this)) - balanceBefore;\n\n    disputeStake = actualReceived;  // Store actual received amount\n    disputer = msg.sender;\n    emit Disputed(reason);\n}\n\nfunction resolveDispute(bool valid) external onlyGovernor {\n    if (disputer == address(0)) revert Errors.NoDispute();\n    uint256 stake = disputeStake;  // Use actual received amount\n    if (valid) {\n        IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(disputer, stake);\n        _revokeTree();\n    } else {\n        IERC20(disputeToken).safeTransfer(msg.sender, stake);\n        endOfDisputePeriod = _endOfDisputePeriod(uint48(block.timestamp));\n    }\n    disputer = address(0);\n    disputeStake = 0;\n    emit DisputeResolved(valid);\n}\n```\n\n### Option 2: Block FoT Tokens in `setDisputeToken()`\n\n```solidity\nfunction setDisputeToken(IERC20 _disputeToken) external onlyGovernor {\n    if (disputer != address(0)) revert Errors.UnresolvedDispute();\n\n    // Test for FoT behavior\n    uint256 testAmount = 1e18;\n    uint256 balanceBefore = _disputeToken.balanceOf(address(this));\n    // Requires governor to have approved testAmount\n    _disputeToken.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), testAmount);\n    uint256 balanceAfter = _disputeToken.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n    if (balanceAfter - balanceBefore != testAmount) {\n        revert Errors.FeeOnTransferNotSupported();\n    }\n\n    // Return test tokens\n    _disputeToken.safeTransfer(msg.sender, balanceAfter - balanceBefore);\n\n    disputeToken = _disputeToken;\n    emit DisputeTokenUpdated(address(_disputeToken));\n}\n```\n\n### Option 3: Document and Restrict\n\nAt minimum, add prominent documentation that FoT tokens must never be used as dispute tokens, and consider adding a token whitelist for dispute tokens similar to the reward token whitelist.",
